value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}+{x}_{3}{d}_{3}+{x}_{4}{d}_{4},$ and ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, ${d}_{3}$, and ${d}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $Dx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4}=1 \\\\ 0=6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the  second equation, we get a false statement $0=6.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119811 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0137f4f1-683a-5532-86ac-a58609ac6c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315122} {:answer/id #uuid "36dddeda-f4aa-5342-a56d-21d473781fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315436} {:answer/id #uuid "40a90e71-399a-5c76-8a51-5bf7d89f38b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315490} {:answer/id #uuid "5eed2d17-3d66-58ef-b9ca-d14343adcf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315652} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5e2b84-4825-5e40-b36f-66a99eaaf9f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36dddeda-f4aa-5342-a56d-21d473781fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315436} :answer-field/id #uuid "4285fcd0-9fe1-5d74-91ff-bd01e5c9f93a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316697}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d2325a17-fb51-5bea-98a4-12b407e10918" :question/math-academy-id "q-34364" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=4 \\\\ 0=-9 \\\\ 11{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a289e23-c521-5e54-87e0-23820eb4b3e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321350} {:answer/id #uuid "204a0a89-e831-51e4-93db-e70840ed8600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321388} {:answer/id #uuid "377c432d-decc-5e5a-9367-f7380ee1dac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321568} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ae17d4-a96f-5105-94cd-190c9f5d420f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322538} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3e4ad3-76a0-55d7-9ad3-a2a4b892bc0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "204a0a89-e831-51e4-93db-e70840ed8600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321388} :answer-field/id #uuid "366ee9e6-9261-50c5-be6e-dbdc9c1112d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfc6c6aa-ca5b-5544-805f-85d28c983b53" :question/math-academy-id "q-35562" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 17 & k-12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-17){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=k+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+5,$ which means that $k=-5.$"}]}
